      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\n`ByteLevelTokenizer.ids_to_text()` passes configured BOS, EOS, and PAD IDs above 255 to `bytes()`, which raises even when those IDs are inside the configured vocabulary.\n\nRemove these configured non-byte IDs before decoding. Preserve existing byte-range behavior, including the default EOS/PAD values, and retain errors for unregistered non-byte IDs below the additional-special-token range.\n\nFixes #8793.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added 27 cases covering BOS/EOS/PAD IDs at 256, 257, and 511, both decoding entry points, repeated specials, UTF-8 text, additional special tokens, byte-range controls, and invalid IDs.\n- Ran those test functions against the actual tokenizer source in an isolated CPU harness: 27 passed. On unchanged main, 19 fail and 8 controls pass. The harness bypasses GPU package initialization and the parent distributed pytest fixtures; this is not a run of the distributed unit suite.\n- `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed. Black, isort, Pylint, and Ruff pass. Its non-blocking mypy step reports the existing `_bos_id: int = None` diagnostic, also reproduced on unchanged main.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nThe GPU distributed suite and model inference were not run on this CPU-only VM. This PR remains a draft pending CI and author review.\n\n## Code provenance\n\nNo code was copied or adapted from another repository.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Relevant unit tests added.\n- [ ] Distributed unit tests completed in the supported GPU environment.\n- [x] Formatting and lint checks run, with the existing mypy diagnostic noted above.\n- [x] Commit has DCO sign-off and an SSH signature.\n- Functional tests, kernel determinism tests, and user documentation: N/A for this tokenizer decoding fix.\n",
